===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[criticize]] or [[rebuke]] (someone).
#: {{syn|en|exprobrate|blame|rebuke|upbraid|Thesaurus:criticize}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|1 Peter|4|14|passage=if ye be '''reproached''' for the name of Christ}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=8|passage=this new commer, Shame, <br>There sit not, and '''reproach''' us as unclean.|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|passage=Mezentius {{...}} with his ardour warmed / His fainting friends, '''reproached''' their shameful flight, / Repelled the victors.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[disgrace]], or bring [[shame]] upon.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Measure|act=V|scene=i|passage=I thought your marriage fit; else imputation, / For that he knew you, might '''reproach''' your life.}}

